 "principles": [
  "Lexical patch only: no new grammar. Every addition is a compound, derivation, diminutive or restored form built by existing rules, except five roots for foundational senses no compound expresses cleanly (decay, stick, poison, flinch, hang).",
  "Where a concept is already sayable, it is documented as a recipe instead of a new word.",
  "Tier 1 = genuine gaps among the report's A-priority senses (plus 'plan', found during testing). Tier 2 = B-priority senses that a short, transparent compound fills."
 ],
